WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:08.940
As international media coverage of

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:10.540
Venezuela increases it seems as if their

00:00:10.559 --> 00:00:12.450
national media coverage of their own

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:14.670
country is actually decreasing. At the

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:16.410
time we were preparing this video we had

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:18.510
a look at the website of Telesur, one of

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:20.070
their largest state-owned television

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:22.859
networks. On the main page they had 29

00:00:22.859 --> 00:00:24.810
headlines and just six of them were

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:26.880
talking about their own country. Despite

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:28.109
what this looks like on the face of

00:00:28.109 --> 00:00:29.640
things though, this couldn't actually

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:31.920
resemble any better what is actually

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:38.010
happening in Venezuela. Today there is no

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:39.570
one who denies that the South American

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:41.129
country is going through one of the

00:00:41.129 --> 00:00:43.200
worst humanitarian crises that the

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.120
entire Continent have ever seen.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:46.950
According to a study run by three

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:48.629
universities from this country, the

00:00:48.629 --> 00:00:50.550
average Venezuelan weighs between nine

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.770
and ten kilos less than two years ago,

00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:55.140
when these food shortages began. Now the

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:56.850
big question is how much blame should be

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:58.500
apportioned to the Venezuelan president

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:00.960
Nicolas Maduro and this is where people

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:04.760
have rather different opinions.

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:08.409
According to many political analysts,

00:01:08.409 --> 00:01:10.600
Venezuela is not a democratic nation

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:12.100
anymore. Things like the President's

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:14.110
attempt to dissolve the Parliament or

00:01:14.110 --> 00:01:15.909
jailing politicians from the opposition

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:18.549
have triggered diplomatic crises at the

00:01:18.549 --> 00:01:20.229
highest level.

00:01:20.229 --> 00:01:22.390
PERU retires their

00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:24.460
ambassador in Venezuela with the support

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:26.049
of their Parliament. Nonetheless there

00:01:26.049 --> 00:01:27.640
are others who still claim that Venezuela

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:30.039
is a democracy. They even say Nicolas

00:01:30.039 --> 00:01:31.899
Maduro, the President, is defending

00:01:31.899 --> 00:01:34.330
himself from a coup d´etat. So the question

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:37.240
here is who is right? Can we say that

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:39.729
Venezuela is a dictatorship or is this

00:01:39.729 --> 00:01:41.860
something of an exaggeration. Today we're

00:01:41.860 --> 00:01:43.539
going to answer this question, but before

00:01:43.539 --> 00:01:45.429
we do let's check out the story of

00:01:45.429 --> 00:01:50.110
Nicolas Maduro and his government say.

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:51.970
WHO is preparing a coup d'etat

00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:53.740
According to Maduro, the Venezuelan

00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:55.990
crisis can be summarized as a conspiracy

00:01:55.990 --> 00:01:58.209
by the United States and their allies to

00:01:58.209 --> 00:02:00.520
destroy the Bolivarian revolution and

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:03.369
the so called 21st century socialism.

00:02:05.649 --> 00:02:07.959
The imperialist elite despises our people

00:02:07.959 --> 00:02:10.000
and have the goal of destroying our

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:13.060
lifestyle, our democracy, our independence

00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:15.940
and our homeland. They have decided to

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:17.950
trigger plans to destabilize the

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:20.560
Venezuelan Society." Oh yes listen... I know

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:22.030
what you're probably thinking but let's

00:02:22.030 --> 00:02:23.980
just imagine for a quick moment that

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:26.019
that theory actually makes some kind of

00:02:26.019 --> 00:02:28.540
sense. In this case the imperialist

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:30.910
elites are not only trying to dismantle

00:02:30.910 --> 00:02:33.549
the Venezuelan economy but also their

00:02:33.549 --> 00:02:35.620
government. And this is what explains

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:37.690
Nicolas Maduro fear of the coup. But

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:39.640
hold on for just a moment because before

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:41.620
we continue we should explain what the

00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:44.109
coup actually means. Well, a coup d'etat

00:02:44.109 --> 00:02:46.540
is defined as the taking of power in a

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:49.030
sudden and violent action carried out by

00:02:49.030 --> 00:02:51.100
a powerful group like the army. And

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:53.519
surprise, surprise! the Venezuelan Army is

00:02:53.519 --> 00:02:57.900
absolutely loyal to Nicolas Maduro.

00:03:00.819 --> 00:03:02.859
This is the father of the Bolivarian

00:03:02.859 --> 00:03:05.469
revolution, Hugo Chavez, used to be a

00:03:05.469 --> 00:03:06.879
member of the military. Unlike other

00:03:06.879 --> 00:03:08.409
countries like the UK where it is

00:03:08.409 --> 00:03:10.689
forbidden by law for soldiers to run for

00:03:10.689 --> 00:03:12.670
office, in Venezuela there are several

00:03:12.670 --> 00:03:14.349
ministers that come from the Armed

00:03:14.349 --> 00:03:16.629
Forces. Here we have Lt. Melendez

00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:18.790
Rivas, the president's chief of staff, or

00:03:18.790 --> 00:03:20.739
the general Marco Rivas, the Minister of

00:03:20.739 --> 00:03:23.349
Food. Actually one third of Maduro's

00:03:23.349 --> 00:03:27.150
government comes from the military.

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:32.310
This being said who could successfully

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:34.830
conduct a coup in Venezuela.

00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:37.440
According to Maduro well as you might've

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:39.300
guessed he suggests this would be his

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:42.000
political opponents. There's only one

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:44.670
problem with this theory though. Not one

00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:46.920
of them have any relationship whatsoever

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:49.470
with the military. People like Enrique

00:03:49.470 --> 00:03:52.140
Capriles, or Leopoldo Lopez, or any of

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:53.700
the other opposition leaders are

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:55.470
professional politicians or former

00:03:55.470 --> 00:03:57.720
businessman... and they have no military

00:03:57.720 --> 00:03:59.670
groups supporting them. Despite all of

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:01.320
this, the government keeps saying that

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:03.210
all these politicians are the real

00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:05.130
instigators all of the countrie's street

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:07.490
violence.

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:12.470
As you can imagine, in a country

00:04:12.470 --> 00:04:14.660
where people need a full day's wages to

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:16.940
get a bag of onions, it's absolutely

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:18.320
normal that people would want to

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:20.870
organize demonstrations... Oh and add to

00:04:20.870 --> 00:04:22.310
this the fact that Caracas is the most

00:04:22.310 --> 00:04:24.440
violent city in all of Latin America and

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:26.630
you'll probably understand why most of

00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:30.400
the protest ends up like this.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:36.170
Nonetheless according to the government

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:37.760
of Venezuela, the clashes between the

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:39.590
police and the protesters and nothing

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:41.470
but the outcome of bourgeoisie propaganda.

00:04:41.470 --> 00:04:43.850
This is why in September of 2015

00:04:44.900 --> 00:04:46.820
Three months before having parliamentary

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:49.220
elections the Venezuelan, police arrested

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:51.410
Leopoldo Lopez, one of the opposition

00:04:51.410 --> 00:04:53.480
leaders the prosecutor claimed that if

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:55.370
man was inciting people into violence

00:04:55.370 --> 00:04:57.230
with these kind of statements made on Twitter.

00:04:57.230 --> 00:05:00.710
'You have the guts to take me to

00:05:00.710 --> 00:05:02.930
prison are you waiting for orders from

00:05:02.930 --> 00:05:05.840
Havana I'm telling you the truth is on

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:08.740
our side'

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:14.010
But the turning point would come later

00:05:14.010 --> 00:05:17.040
in December of 2015. At this time,

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:19.260
Venezuela has parliamentary elections

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:21.389
and as you can imagine the opposition

00:05:21.389 --> 00:05:23.910
party is unified in the so-called Table

00:05:23.910 --> 00:05:27.240
of Democratic Unity, AKA the MUD, beat

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:30.630
Maduro party by over 2 million votes. The

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:32.280
president's reaction was actually what

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:33.780
you'd expect from every Democratic leader.

00:05:33.780 --> 00:05:37.350
'We have recognized

00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:39.840
this outcome even if we don't like it

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:42.750
that we accept it and we say that

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:45.240
democracy and the Constitution are the

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:47.760
real winners here' But the hold on for

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:50.130
just a moment because this is when the

00:05:50.130 --> 00:05:52.169
problem starts this brand-new

00:05:52.169 --> 00:05:53.820
anti-government Parliament started

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:56.580
trying to impeach the president and this

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:58.440
is when all of a sudden Maduro and his

00:05:58.440 --> 00:06:01.620
ministers made a radical shift. t

00:06:01.620 --> 00:06:03.419
'This economic war

00:06:03.419 --> 00:06:05.430
had influence of a big share of our

00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:08.220
population and this turned the public

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:10.350
opinion'. During this time, Nicolas Maduro

00:06:10.350 --> 00:06:12.600
tried to dissolve Parliament. According

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:14.400
to his government, some of those MPs had

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:15.930
been elected by cheating in the

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:18.000
electoral process. But not even the

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:20.310
Supreme Court of Venezuela accepted

00:06:20.310 --> 00:06:22.350
this version. This is why on May the 1st

00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:23.610
2017,

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:26.780
Maduro made his final decision.

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:33.750
'I'm calling up the constitutional power to

00:06:33.750 --> 00:06:36.990
get the peace this republic needs to

00:06:36.990 --> 00:06:39.180
beat the fascist coup and let the people

00:06:39.180 --> 00:06:41.790
bring the harmony and the actual

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:44.220
national dialogue'. In other words, Maduro

00:06:44.220 --> 00:06:45.960
wants a new Parliament to write a brand

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:47.790
new Vonstitution which would give him

00:06:47.790 --> 00:06:50.580
unlimited power and this would be the

00:06:50.580 --> 00:06:52.260
ultimate step for creating a

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:54.480
dictatorship. And as you might well now

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:56.640
wonder... Is this going to be through an

00:06:56.640 --> 00:06:59.270
election?

00:07:01.050 --> 00:07:04.060
Well... theoretically yes but the truth is

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:06.520
that, since 2015, there are lots of

00:07:06.520 --> 00:07:09.250
opposition leaders behind bars.

00:07:09.250 --> 00:07:10.900
The Maduro

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:12.580
supporters say that Venezuela has

00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:14.440
freedom of speech but is this really

00:07:14.440 --> 00:07:20.020
true? Well that's a look at that.

00:07:20.020 --> 00:07:23.139
'Is there freedom of speech in Venezuela?'

00:07:23.139 --> 00:07:24.970
According to the current Venezuelan Constitution,

00:07:24.970 --> 00:07:27.789
freedom of speech is a fundamental right.

00:07:27.789 --> 00:07:29.800
And yes there are many newspapers who

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:31.930
oppose the government but guess what,

00:07:31.930 --> 00:07:33.639
the problem these newspapers have is...

00:07:33.639 --> 00:07:35.530
Well they don't actually have any paper

00:07:35.530 --> 00:07:39.449
on which to print their news.

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:43.390
Just like that. In Venezuela, paper is a

00:07:43.390 --> 00:07:45.790
monopoly regulated by the state and this

00:07:45.790 --> 00:07:47.800
is why a media outlets like El Nacional,

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:50.320
which is contrary to Maduro, has to

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:52.390
reduce their circulation and even the

00:07:52.390 --> 00:07:54.850
number of pages in their newspaper. Other

00:07:54.850 --> 00:07:56.350
dailies have had to become weeklies

00:07:56.350 --> 00:07:57.850
because they couldn't print so many

00:07:57.850 --> 00:07:59.170
papers. And now you might be wondering...

00:07:59.170 --> 00:08:01.180
Well... what about the internet. I mean

00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:03.580
who's in reads print papers anymore? Well...

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:05.590
unfortunately, Maduro and his governments

00:08:05.590 --> 00:08:07.480
have an absolute power to block any

00:08:07.480 --> 00:08:09.310
website. At the other hand of the site of

00:08:09.310 --> 00:08:11.080
Bit.ly. This is a site where you

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:12.610
could put the links at any page and it

00:08:12.610 --> 00:08:14.170
makes it shorter so you can tweet it

00:08:14.170 --> 00:08:14.830
easily.

00:08:14.830 --> 00:08:16.630
Does it sound counter-revolutionary to

00:08:16.630 --> 00:08:21.310
you? well check this out. 'Bit.ly shortcuts are

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:23.290
banned in Venezuela' As you can imagine,

00:08:23.290 --> 00:08:25.420
if bit.ly is forbidden, other critical

00:08:25.420 --> 00:08:27.880
websites like CNN,  Dollars today or InfoBAE

00:08:27.880 --> 00:08:30.010
are also banned.

00:08:30.010 --> 00:08:31.600
if you live in Venezuela and you want to

00:08:31.600 --> 00:08:33.280
visit these websites you must do it

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:35.710
through a proxy. Just like in China. And

00:08:35.710 --> 00:08:37.000
of course don't forget that there have

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:39.280
been more than 40 journalists threatened

00:08:39.280 --> 00:08:43.150
by the government's allies or even worse...

00:08:43.150 --> 00:08:46.280
'Six Twitter users are in jail in

00:08:46.280 --> 00:08:48.320
Venezuela for giving their political

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:50.480
opinions'. Yep... you have that right. They

00:08:50.480 --> 00:08:52.850
are not being judged or fined... they are

00:08:52.850 --> 00:08:55.220
in prison. But hold on for just a minute

00:08:55.220 --> 00:08:57.410
because all of this is nothing compared

00:08:57.410 --> 00:08:59.480
to what's happening in television.

00:09:00.760 --> 00:09:05.180
During decades, Caracas was

00:09:05.180 --> 00:09:06.740
the Hollywood of South American soap

00:09:06.740 --> 00:09:09.050
operas. Venezuela was famous for having

00:09:09.050 --> 00:09:11.360
lots of private TV stations and, of

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:12.740
course, some of them were contrary to

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:14.840
the Government. The Venezuelan

00:09:14.840 --> 00:09:16.880
Constitution provides the freedom of

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:19.070
speech on TV but, on the other hand, the

00:09:19.070 --> 00:09:21.170
law forces them to broadcast all of the

00:09:21.170 --> 00:09:23.060
president's speeches. And we're not

00:09:23.060 --> 00:09:24.680
talking about one show a year.

00:09:24.680 --> 00:09:27.590
Maduro appears on TV several times a

00:09:27.590 --> 00:09:29.900
week and the TVs have to make a break,

00:09:29.900 --> 00:09:32.570
no matter their schedule, and broadcast the

00:09:32.570 --> 00:09:34.460
presidential speech. Sometimes, these

00:09:34.460 --> 00:09:37.130
speeches can last for hours. Add to

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:42.050
this other stories like this.

00:09:42.050 --> 00:09:44.960
'Globovision, a Venezuelan TV broadcaster, is

00:09:44.960 --> 00:09:47.420
sold to a new owner who promises a new

00:09:47.420 --> 00:09:50.660
more moderate ideology'. Before Maduro was

00:09:50.660 --> 00:09:52.340
the president... during the time of Hugo Chavez,

00:09:52.340 --> 00:09:53.690
Globovision

00:09:53.690 --> 00:09:56.240
was a die-hard anti-government TV

00:09:56.240 --> 00:09:58.100
station. But all of a sudden it was sold

00:09:58.100 --> 00:10:00.740
in 2013. And new owners had close ties

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:02.720
with the president. So the first thing

00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:04.250
they did when taken the later control of the

00:10:04.250 --> 00:10:06.200
company was to fire half of the staff.

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:08.330
And then, surprise surprise!

00:10:08.330 --> 00:10:12.910
Globovision became a 'centrist' station.

00:10:13.040 --> 00:10:16.080
But make no mistake. This is merely one

00:10:16.080 --> 00:10:18.750
example. Today there is almost no media

00:10:18.750 --> 00:10:20.400
in Venezuela that is critical of the

00:10:20.400 --> 00:10:22.230
Government. So the question I would now

00:10:22.230 --> 00:10:24.900
like to ask you is... What exactly is

00:10:24.900 --> 00:10:26.880
the difference between Nicolas Maduro

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:30.000
and any other dictator? Can anybody claim

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:31.770
Venezuela is still really a democracy?

00:10:31.770 --> 00:10:33.900
Well we'd love to know what you think

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:35.940
You can let us know in the comment

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:36.690
section below.

